{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EPH",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Honor thy father and mother (which is the first commandment with promise)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Servants, be obedient to them that are ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as to Christ;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not with eye-service, as men-pleasers; but as the servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With good will doing service, as to the Lord, and not to men:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing that whatever good thing any man doeth, the same will he receive from the Lord, whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bond or free.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And, ye masters, do the same things to them, forbearing threatening: knowing that your Master also is in heaven; neither is there respect of persons with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put on the whole armor of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "places",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore take to you the whole armor of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breast-plate of righteousness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Above all, taking the shield of faith, with which ye will be able to extinguish all the fiery darts of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching for this purpose with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And for me, that utterance may be given to me, that I may open my mouth boldly, to make known the mystery of the gospel,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For which I am an embassador in bonds: that therein I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But that ye also may know my affairs, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " how I do, Tychicus, a beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, will make known to you all things:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom I have sent to you for the same purpose, that ye may know our affairs, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he may comfort your hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Peace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the brethren, and love with faith from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EPH.6.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EPH.6.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with all them that love our Lord Jesus Christ in sincerity. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
